# ARCHIVE RULES

The archive grows through consistency.

Every future collection must respect the principles established by the archive.

---

## COLLECTION REQUIREMENTS

Every collection must include:

Concept

Meaning

Symbol

Color System

Front System

Back System

Packaging

Lifestyle Direction

---

## SYMBOL REQUIREMENTS

Every collection must possess its own symbol.

The symbol must communicate the concept.

The symbol must not duplicate existing archive symbols.

---

## COLOR REQUIREMENTS

Colors must support meaning.

Color decisions are conceptual.

Not trend-driven.

---

## GARMENT REQUIREMENTS

All collections must follow the approved garment system.

Changes require archive approval.

---

## BRAND MARK REQUIREMENTS

RARO MARK belongs to the archive.

Collection symbols belong to collections.

The two must never be confused.

---

## EXPANSION PRINCIPLE

New collections may be added.

However, every new collection must answer:

What is the mark?

What is the meaning?

Why does it belong in the archive?

If these questions cannot be answered clearly, the collection does not enter the archive.

---

## FINAL PRINCIPLE

RARO is not a catalog of garments.

RARO is an archive of marks.

The garment is the medium.

The mark is the message.
